    "body": "## Purpose\n\nIn the InternLM2 tool parser's non-streaming `extract_tool_calls`, when the\nparsed tool name is not among the request's `tools`, the code builds an\n`ExtractedToolCallInformation(tools_called=False, ...)` but never returns it.\nExecution falls through and the unlisted tool is emitted as a real tool call\nanyway, so a hallucinated / unlisted tool name bypasses the tool whitelist.\n\n```python\nif not tools or name not in [t.function.name for t in tools]:\n    ExtractedToolCallInformation(tools_called=False, ...)   # built, never returned\n# ... falls through and returns tools_called=True\n```\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add the missing `return`.\n- Change the condition from `not tools or` to `tools and` so the whitelist is\n  only enforced when tools are actually provided. The batch API constructs the\n  parser with `tools=None` (`batch_serving.py`), and returning early on an empty\n  tool list would otherwise drop every tool call in batch mode.\n\nNet behavior:\n- tools provided + unlisted name -> not emitted (the fix)\n- tools provided + listed name -> emitted (unchanged)\n- no tools provided (batch) -> emitted (no regression)\n\n## Test\n\nAdds regression tests to `tests/tool_parsers/test_internlm2_tool_parser.py`\ncovering all three cases above.\n",
